 class="rj2ep81"><div class="rj2ep87"><div class="_1jiz7rn0 _1jiz7rn1"><div class="_1jiz7rn7"><img alt="Emma Roth" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="_4aoxp34" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/author_profile_images/195810/EMMA_ROTH.0.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/author_profile_images/195810/EMMA_ROTH.0.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/author_profile_images/195810/EMMA_ROTH.0.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96" style="color: transparent;"></div><div class="_1jiz7rn2 _1jiz7rn3"><span class="_1jiz7rn6">Emma Roth</span><span class="duet--article--timestamp g4xafw2 g4xafw0 _19wv7tc5 _1jiz7rna"><time datetime="2026-10-29T20:57:13+00:00">Two hours ago</time></span></div></div><div class="_4ine551 _4ine550"><div class="_4ine554">Google is sunsetting its AI coding agent, Jules.</div><div class="_1y5ugvbf _1y5ugvb0"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1">The company launched Jules <a href="/2024/12/11/24318628/jules-google-ai-coding-agent-gemini-2-0-announcement">in December 2024</a>, positioning it as a tool that can complete coding jobs “you don’t want to do.” But now, Jules is shutting down, and <a href="https://x.com/julesagent/status/2115883717705261283">Google says</a> it will bring its learnings from the tool into its AI coding platform, Antigravity:</p></div><div class="_1y5ugvbg"><blockquote class="duet--article--blockquote _1lkuyz84 _1lkuyz81 _1lkuyz80 _19wv7tc9"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup _1lkuyz8b _1lkuyz88">We’re working on bringing our learnings from Jules into <a href="https://x.com/antigravity">@antigravity</a> s