%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/author_profile_images/195784/ADI_ROBERTSON.0.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></div><div class="_1jiz7rn2 _1jiz7rn3"><span class="_1jiz7rn6">Adi Robertson</span><span class="duet--article--timestamp g4xafw2 g4xafw0 _19wv7tc5 _1jiz7rna"><time datetime="2026-10-29T18:27:54+00:00">Oct 29</time></span></div></div><div class="_4ine551 _4ine550"><div class="_4ine554">An AO3 disaster.</div><div class="_1y5ugvbf _1y5ugvb0"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1">Fanworks hub Archive of Our Own is no stranger to downtime, but an as-yet-unexplained outage of potentially up to a month — announced on the <a href="https://www.otwstatus.org/incidents/g12jnxck9g6h">site’s status page</a> — is going to send a lot of fanfic writers scrambling:</p></div><div class="_1y5ugvbg"><blockquote class="duet--article--blockquote _1lkuyz84 _1lkuyz81 _1lkuyz80 _19wv7tc9"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup _1lkuyz8b _1lkuyz88">We estimate that service restoration for #AO3 will take around 2 weeks but it could be up to 4 weeks. We are hopeful that we will be able to bring the site back up in a degraded state sooner. If that does happen, there may be times when the site has to be brought down temporarily until this is fully resolved. Please stay tuned for further info.</p></blockquote></div></div><div class="_1p001ee0"><div class="_1y5ugvbe"><div class="_1y5ugvb9"><a class="_1y5ugvba" href="https://www.otwstatus.org/incidents/g12jnxck9g6h" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AO3 Down for Maintenance</a><p class="_1y5ugvbb">[<!-- -->OTW Status<!-- -->]</p></div></div></div></div><div class="dq5wa40"><span class="dq5wa41"><span class="_4zezgs7 _4zezgs2"><a class="duet--article--comments-link _4zezgsc" href="/tech/1022506/an-ao3-disaster#comments"><svg class="_4ze