l="Sure enough, the FCC just banned Chinese labs from testing US-bound gadgets." class="rj2ep88" href="/policy/1022439/sure-enough-the-fcc-just-banned-chinese-labs-from-testing-us-bound-gadgets"></a><div class="rj2ep81"><div class="rj2ep87"><div class="_1jiz7rn0 _1jiz7rn1"><div class="_1jiz7rn7"><img alt="Sean Hollister" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="_4aoxp34" style="color:transparent" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></div><div class="_1jiz7rn2 _1jiz7rn3"><span class="_1jiz7rn6">Sean Hollister</span><span class="duet--article--timestamp g4xafw2 g4xafw0 _19wv7tc5 _1jiz7rna"><time datetime="2026-10-29T18:03:37+00:00">Oct 29</time></span></div></div><div class="_4ine551 _4ine550"><div class="_4ine554">Sure enough, the FCC just banned Chinese labs from testing US-bound gadgets.</div><div class="_1y5ugvbf _1y5ugvb0"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1">“Starting 2 years from now, we will only allow for Test Labs to be based in the U.S or “Reciprocal Economies,” i.e. those places that are willing to recognize U.S.-based testing,” <a href="https://x.com/FCC/status/2115831011636604970">writes FCC chair Brendan Carr</a>. His stated reasoning makes some sense, but it also omits important context: today’s test labs <a href="/policy/1009258/the-fcc-plans-to-ban-all-chinese-labs-from-testing-us-gadgets-by-2029">are concentrated in China</a> because that’s where gadgets are made.</p></div></div><div class="_1p00