y’s license plate readers." class="rj2ep88" href="/tech/1022195/la-is-just-replacing-flock-with-a-different-companys-license-plate-readers"></a><div class="rj2ep81"><div class="rj2ep87"><div class="_1jiz7rn0 _1jiz7rn1"><div class="_1jiz7rn7"><img alt="Terrence O'Brien" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="_4aoxp34" style="color:transparent" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></div><div class="_1jiz7rn2 _1jiz7rn3"><span class="_1jiz7rn6">Terrence O'Brien</span><span class="duet--article--timestamp g4xafw2 g4xafw0 _19wv7tc5 _1jiz7rna"><time datetime="2026-10-29T14:54:43+00:00">Oct 29</time></span></div></div><div class="_4ine551 _4ine550"><div class="_4ine554">LA is just replacing Flock with a different company’s license plate readers.</div><div class="_1y5ugvbf _1y5ugvb0"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1">In July, the LAPD <a href="/tech/964903/the-lapd-has-suspended-its-use-of-flocks-license-plate-readers-for-now">suspended its use of Flock’s cameras</a> over concerns about how the company was handling its data. Now it’s rolling out <a href="https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-10-29/flock-safety-lapd-axon-contract">hundreds of ALPRs from competitor Axon</a>. The company has so far escaped the backlash Flock faced, but it’ll likely face growing scrutiny as it fills the gaps left by canceled Flock contracts.</p></div></div><div class="_1p001ee0"><div class="_1y5ugvbe"><div class="_1y5u